---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, tools, categories } from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="About BestSoftwareGuides" description={`Who runs ${site.name}, how we make money and how we keep rankings independent.`} path="/about/">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About {site.name}</h1>
    <p>{site.name} is an independent software directory. We track {tools.length} tools across {categories.length} categories and publish ranked lists, plan-by-plan pricing and head-to-head comparisons.</p>
    <p>Our rule is simple: <strong>every number on the page can be checked.</strong> Prices link to the vendor's own pricing page and show the date we checked them. Scores come from a <a href="/methodology/">published formula</a>.</p>
    <h2>Editorial team</h2>
    {/* TODO(owner): add the real names, roles and experience of the people who research and edit the site.
        Named, credible authors are one of the strongest trust signals for readers and search engines. */}
    <p>The {site.editor.name} researches each category, reads every vendor's own pricing page, and records the price, plan limits and the date it was checked. Records are re-checked on a schedule, and anything we cannot confirm is marked "Not confirmed" rather than guessed. Spotted an error? <a href="/contact/">Send a correction</a>.</p>
    <h2>How we make money</h2>
    <p>Some outbound links may be affiliate links, and some rankings place a featured partner above its score position with a "Featured partner" label. Neither changes any tool's score, and every other tool stays in score order. See our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> for corrections or questions.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
